</comment>
                            <comment id="492243" author="bodgerer" created="Wed, 1 Apr 2026 10:05:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi @Jian Yu,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks for this: I&apos;ve cherry picked those three patches onto a fresh 2.15.8 checkout with mixed results. I see a successful configure on EL 9.7 (doca 3.2.1 / aarch64+64k) but unfortunately get this on EL 8.10 (doca 3.2.1 / ppc64le):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
sh autogen.sh &amp;amp;&amp;amp; ./configure --with-linux=/usr/src/kernels/$(uname -r)
...
==============================================================================
checking whether to enable tunable backoff TCP support... yes
checking &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; Linux kernel has tunable backoff TCP support... no
checking whether to use Compat RDMA... /usr/bin/ofed_info
configure: error:
You seem to have an OFED installed but have not installed it&apos;s devel &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;package&lt;/span&gt;.
If you still want to build Lustre &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; your OFED I/B stack, you need to install its devel headers RPM.
Instead, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; you want to build Lustre &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; your kernel&apos;s built-in I/B stack rather than your installed OFED stack, either remove the OFED &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;package&lt;/span&gt;(s) or use --with-o2ib=no.&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Problem seems to be that ${target_cpu} resolves to powerpc64le instead of ppc64le on a ppc64le system?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="492283" author="yujian" created="Wed, 1 Apr 2026 16:51:29 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thank you &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=bodgerer&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;bodgerer&quot;&gt;bodgerer&lt;/a&gt; for verifying the patches. Could you please try to replace the &lt;b&gt;${target_cpu}&lt;/b&gt; with &lt;b&gt;$(uname -m)&lt;/b&gt; in lnet/autoconf/lustre-lnet.m4 to see if it works?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="492321" author="bodgerer" created="Thu, 2 Apr 2026 12:51:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi Yian Yu,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yes: if I replace $O2IBDIR_PATH/${target_cpu}/${LINUXRELEASE} with $O2IBDIR_PATH/${target_cpu}/${LINUXRELEASE} on both matching lines, I get a successful configure &amp;amp; make on both ppc64le and aarch64+64k.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mark&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
